Bootstrap: localimage
From: calicityper-tools.sif

# CaliciTyper itself, on top of the tools image: ONE artifact that runs the
# tool, rather than "sif + a host conda env + a host Python".
#
# Build both from the repository root, in this order. `localimage` and the
# %files paths below are resolved against the current directory, so
# calicityper-tools.sif has to sit in the repo root at build time (the built
# copy currently lives in ../calicityper_runs/):
#
#   apptainer build calicityper-tools.sif containers/calicityper-tools.def
#   apptainer build calicityper.sif       containers/calicityper.def
#
# Built from the tools image rather than from python:3.11 again, so the pinned
# BLAST/MAFFT/OpenRDP %post is not duplicated and the two images cannot drift.
# The tools image pins its own base by digest; this one inherits that.
#
# Reference data is NOT baked in. `calicityper setup` fetches ~GB from Zenodo
# (doi:10.5281/zenodo.24161236) and verifies it, and writing that into the
# image would be a post-build write into a read-only artifact. config.py
# therefore defaults DATA to /data inside a container, which is the bind mount
# below. An explicit CALICITYPER_DATA still wins.

%files
    pyproject.toml /opt/calicityper-src/pyproject.toml
    README.md      /opt/calicityper-src/README.md
    calicityper    /opt/calicityper-src/calicityper

%labels
    Description   CaliciTyper + BLAST+, MAFFT, OpenRDP
    Entrypoint    calicityper
    Data.mount    /data   (bind a host copy of the Zenodo reference set here)
    Data.setup    apptainer exec -B ./refdata:/data calicityper.sif calicityper setup
    # Inherited from calicityper-tools.sif, repeated so one `inspect` shows it:
    Tools         blastn, makeblastdb, mafft, clustalw2, iqtree, openrdp
    Cpu.default   1
    Cpu.useful    4

%post
    set -eu
    # 1: the mount point has to exist in the image for -B /data to land.
    mkdir -p /data
    # 2: install from the copied source, not from PyPI, so the image matches
    #    the tree it was built from. Dependency pins live in pyproject.toml.
    pip install --no-cache-dir /opt/calicityper-src
    # 3: fail the build, not the first run, if the entry point is missing.
    calicityper --help > /dev/null

%environment
    export LC_ALL=C
    # CALICITYPER_DATA deliberately unset: config.py defaults to /data in a
    # container, and leaving it unset keeps an explicit override working.

%test
    set -e
    calicityper --help > /dev/null && echo "calicityper ok"
    blastn -version | head -1
    mafft --version
    openrdp --help > /dev/null && echo "openrdp ok"

%runscript
    # Single entry point, arguments passed straight through: one container,
    # one concern. `apptainer exec` still reaches the tools directly.
    exec calicityper "$@"

%help
    CaliciTyper with its external tools, in one image.

    Reference data lives on a bind mount, not in the image:

      mkdir -p refdata
      apptainer exec -B ./refdata:/data calicityper.sif calicityper setup
      apptainer run  -B ./refdata:/data calicityper.sif --help

    Any writable path works; /data is only the default inside the container.
    To use a reference copy elsewhere, set CALICITYPER_DATA:

      apptainer exec -B /scratch:/scratch --env CALICITYPER_DATA=/scratch/ref \
          calicityper.sif calicityper ...

    All five external tools are present: blastn, makeblastdb, mafft,
    clustalw2 and iqtree (3.1.4, installed as `iqtree`/`iqtree3`, not
    `iqtree2`), plus openrdp in its own interpreter. CALICITYPER_IQTREE and
    CALICITYPER_CLUSTALW still override if you want host binaries.

    One core by default; MAFFT and IQ-TREE thread, and about four is the
    useful ceiling. Outputs go to stdout and to whatever output path you pass, so
    redirect rather than looking for log files inside the container.
